(1) KRAWTCHOUK-MOMENT EXTREMALITY: does consec maximize each binding M_j(E)?
================================================================================================
  For each k, the binding moments are j with c_j>0.  We sweep bounded spread and
  report, per binding j, whether consec is the max of M_j (and the # of beaters).

  k=8  (maxE<=16, 11440 sets):  binding j=[2, 4]
    M_2: consec=6.12109  windowmax=6.12109  consec_is_max=True  beaters=0  (argmax=consec)
    M_4: consec=3.80544  windowmax=3.80544  consec_is_max=True  beaters=0  (argmax=consec)
    L_y: consec=0.35823  windowmax=0.35823  consec_is_max=True  beaters=0  cap=0.38146  L_y(consec)<=cap:True

  k=9  (maxE<=15, 6435 sets):  binding j=[1, 2, 3]
