================================================================================================
(2) COMPLEMENTARY SLACKNESS: consec's occupancy p_t vs the dual binding set.
================================================================================================
  Dual tight cells = {t: g(t)=1[t=0]}.  LP-optimal primal supported there.
  We list consec p_t, mark which cells are slack (g(t)>1[t=0]), and the mass consec
  puts on slack cells (= why L_y(consec) exceeds measS7(consec)).

  k=8: consec p_t = ['481/1470', '359/1470', '25/147', '26/245', '17/210', '5/98', '1/49']
       float p_t   = [0.3272, 0.2442, 0.1701, 0.1061, 0.081, 0.051, 0.0204]
       tight cells=[0, 1, 2, 4, 5]  slack cells=[3, 6]
       consec mass on slack cells = 0.12653  (p_t on slack: [(3, 0.1061), (6, 0.0204)])
       => consec saturates LP support? (zero mass on slack): False

