================================================================================================
(3) LP TIGHTNESS: gap L_y(consec) - measS7(consec), decomposed over slack cells.
================================================================================================
  L_y - measS7 = sum_t g(t)p_t - p_0 = sum_{t>=1} g(t)p_t  (since g(0)=1).
  This is the EXACT non-tightness.  measS7=L_y iff p_t=0 for all t>=1 with g(t)>0.

  k=8: measS7=0.32721  L_y=0.35823  gap=0.03102=38/1225
       gap contributions g(t)p_t (t>=1): [(3, '13/1225'), (6, '1/49')]
       tight at consec (gap=0)? False

  k=9: measS7=0.41616  L_y=0.49288  gap=0.07672=29/378
       gap contributions g(t)p_t (t>=1): [(1, '653/10584'), (4, '13/1764'), (5, '3/392')]
       tight at consec (gap=0)? False

  k=10: measS7=0.50448  L_y=0.57008  gap=0.06560=2083/31752
       gap contributions g(t)p_t (t>=1): [(1, '551/10584'), (4, '55/7938'), (5, '5/756')]
       tight at consec (gap=0)? False

  k=11: measS7=0.58146  L_y=0.68305  gap=0.10159=32/315
       gap contributions g(t)p_t (t>=1): [(1, '1283/17640'), (2, '827/52920'), (5, '23/3780'), (6, '1/140')]
       tight at consec (gap=0)? False

  k=12: measS7=0.62411  L_y=0.71417  gap=0.09006=104849/1164240
